<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">I don't intend to lose, my love</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Adora pulled one of Entraptaâ€™s bots out of her bag and felt a pang of guilt as she rigged the stolen bot to self-destruct. She felt bad for deceiving the other princesses, but they would understand eventually why she had to do this. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She should have known it would all go wrong. It could have been the dark supply tent, or her steadily rising fever, or the adrenaline of a stealth mission. Either way, as Adora went to rig the third bot, her finger missed the â€œRemote control detonationâ€ option and accidentally pressed â€œImmediate detonation.â€ All she remembers is her heart rate skyrocketing and the overwhelming urge to move before her world erupted into flames.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When Adora finally regained consciousness, she was so sore that she almost forgot the reason why she had come there in the first place. That is, until she heard a familiar voice rise above the ringing in her ears.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œYou sure do like to make an entrance, donâ€™t you, Adora?â€&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>immortalvessel</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
